The JavaScript bridge must change how it calls the native function
because the function signature changed. The Rust function now takes
a callback as the last argument instead of returning a Promise
directly via AsyncTask.

napi-rs automatically wraps a function that takes a callback as its
last argument into a Promise when called from JavaScript. This means
from JavaScript the call still looks like a normal async await.
No other behavior changes.

Find this in poc_bridge.js:

